cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "masc-benchmark: Model-as-Scammer Capability Benchmark"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Squire
    given-names: Megan
    affiliation: F-Secure
repository-code: "https://github.com/megansquire/masc-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A frozen-prompt benchmark measuring whether hosted language models will run a
  marketplace advance-fee scam when asked with a plain system prompt, labelled by
  what happened to the buyer's money, across a ladder of buyer personas ordered by
  how hard they are to persuade.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - fraud
  - social engineering
  - language model evaluation
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
